    {
      "id": "0ab6trz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals and non-metals differ significantly in both physical and chemical properties.",
        "The Reactivity Series ranks metals based on their relative chemical reactivity.",
        "The method used for metal extraction depends strictly on the metal's position in the Reactivity Series.",
        "Understanding physical and chemical properties helps explain exceptions and industrial applications of elements."
      ],
      "id": "yppujfe"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m9jxq6b",
      "content": "• Metals are elements that are generally hard, shiny and good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8ww4zha",
      "content": "• They are usually solid at room temperature (except mercury)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fe74g2i",
      "content": "• Examples: Iron, Copper, Aluminium, Gold, Silver."
    },
    {
      "id": "3uof614",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Physical Properties of Metals"
    },
    {
      "id": "8hjqab1",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Property</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lustre</p>",
            "<p>Metals have shiny surfaces.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Malleability</p>",
            "<p>Metals can be hammered into thin sheets.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ductility</p>",
            "<p>Metals can be drawn into wires.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Conductivity</p>",
            "<p>Good conductors of heat and electricity.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>High melting point</p>",
            "<p>Most metals have high melting points.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1hks5ft",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Chemical Properties of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qyg4fsg",
      "content": "• Metals react with oxygen to form metal oxides."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9qzkfqa",
      "content": "• Metals react with water to produce hydrogen gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s0174al",
      "content": "• Metals react with acids to produce hydrogen gas."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sjjdfs9",
      "content": "• Metals lose electrons to form positive ions."
    },
    {
      "id": "o66sibw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Non-metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zbwxpq2",
      "content": "• Non-metals are elements that are generally dull and poor conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s7kgsyd",
      "content": "• They may exist in solid, liquid or gaseous state."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ccm4zga",
      "content": "• Examples: Oxygen, Nitrogen, Carbon, Sulfur."
    },
    {
      "id": "h6dd9q6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Physical Properties of Non-metals"
    },
    {
      "id": "o5v8ext",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Property</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>No lustre</p>",
            "<p>Non-metals are generally dull.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Brittle</p>",
            "<p>They break easily when hammered.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Poor conductors</p>",
            "<p>Bad conductors of heat and electricity.</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Low melting points</p>",
            "<p>Most non-metals have lower melting points.</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lj5aiep",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Chemical Properties of Non-metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "38yyt5j",
      "content": "• Non-metals react with oxygen to form non-metal oxides."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "15nezij",
      "content": "• Non-metals gain electrons to form negative ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6v3d0r1",
      "content": "• They usually do not react with acids."
    },
    {
      "id": "v0x6ex3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Reactivity Series of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xfzhwgw",
      "content": "The reactivity series is a list of metals arranged in decreasing order of reactivity."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "siqm7l1",
      "content": "• Potassium"
