    {
      "id": "o7jezmj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequently tested: Exceptions in physical properties (e.g., Mercury as a liquid metal, Graphite as a conducting non-metal).",
        "High priority: Predicting displacement reaction outcomes using the Reactivity Series.",
        "Key distinction: Differences between Calcination and Roasting in metal extraction processes."
      ],
      "id": "tjs4kaa"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pjhc8gr",
      "content": "• Highly reactive metals are extracted by electrolysis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b8oolw1",
      "content": "• Moderately reactive metals are extracted by reduction using carbon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6yxby0a",
      "content": "• Less reactive metals are often found in free state."
    },
    {
      "id": "5ksvse0",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6fjahlt",
      "content": "• Metals are good conductors of heat and electricity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3pj64i",
      "content": "• Non-metals are generally poor conductors."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vugt2o4",
      "content": "• Mercury is the only metal that is liquid at room temperature."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "94natsp",
      "content": "• Gold and silver are least reactive metals."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
